cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RX150 Hedge Algebra Control"
message: >-
  Nếu bạn dùng phần mềm này trong công bố khoa học, xin trích dẫn theo siêu dữ liệu dưới đây.
  If you use this software in academic work, please cite it using the metadata below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Tran"
    given-names: "Nguyen Binh"
    alias: nguyenbinh-shark
repository-code: "https://github.com/nguyenbinh-shark/RX150_Hedge_Algebra_Control"
abstract: >-
  A ROS 2 Humble workspace for the Interbotix ReactorX-150 manipulator that moves the joint
  position loop out of Dynamixel firmware and onto the host at 100 Hz in PWM mode, so that
  control laws become swappable and directly comparable. Three controllers occupy the same
  slot: a type-1 Mamdani fuzzy controller with Pinocchio gravity compensation, the same
  fuzzy PD with kinematic velocity/acceleration feedforward, and a Hedge Algebra Controller
  (HAC) whose entire control surface reduces to three scalar coefficients. The workspace
  also contains YOLO-segmentation tube detection, MediaPipe gesture interaction, AprilTag
  hand-eye calibration, and hardware identification tooling for gravity and friction models.
keywords:
  - hedge algebra
  - fuzzy control
  - robot manipulator
  - ROS 2
  - Interbotix RX150
  - gravity compensation
  - PWM control
  - human-robot interaction
license: BSD-3-Clause
